  "notes": "ごちそう combines the honorific ご with {馳走|ちそう} (originally meaning 'running around' to prepare a meal).\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ごちそうさまでした: thank you for the meal (after eating)\n- ごちそうする: to treat someone to a meal\n- ごちそうになる: to be treated to a meal\n\nUSAGE:\n- Used both as a noun (delicious food) and with する (to treat someone)",
